WEBVTT

00:07.200 --> 00:08.300
<b>Ready?</b>

00:08.300 --> 00:09.460
<b>Now watch this.</b>

00:10.120 --> 00:13.590
<b>When the gauge lights up,
press down, and you'll get a combo.</b>

00:13.590 --> 00:16.100
<b>This way, you can get materials
without taking damage.</b>

00:16.100 --> 00:18.590
<b>Wow! Big Bro, you rock!</b>

00:22.600 --> 00:24.560
<b>If only you could pour all that passion</b>

00:24.560 --> 00:27.900
<b>into your studies or sports
instead of video games.</b>

00:27.900 --> 00:30.070
<b>It'd make your mother so happy.</b>

00:30.070 --> 00:31.150
<b>Uh...</b>

00:31.150 --> 00:33.220
<b>Oh, I don't see the harm.</b>

00:33.770 --> 00:38.990
<b>Of course. Just like someone I know
who pours all his passion into work,</b>

00:38.990 --> 00:41.830
<b>putting his family
in the back seat, right?</b>

00:41.830 --> 00:45.330
<b>Who could that be?</b>

00:45.330 --> 00:46.940
<b>But you know what...</b>

00:47.500 --> 00:50.500
<b>Here we are, going camping
because I finally got some time off.</b>

00:50.500 --> 00:53.090
<b>Of course it would start raining!</b>

00:53.090 --> 00:55.380
<b>Sorry, you guys.</b>

00:55.380 --> 00:57.910
<b>Hey, no, it's all right.</b>

00:58.340 --> 01:00.430
<b>Big Bro, my turn!</b>

01:00.430 --> 01:04.190
<b>No way! I'm gonna keep playing
till I finish this quest!</b>

01:04.190 --> 01:05.500
<b>Come on!</b>

01:40.700 --> 01:47.460
<b>MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY</b>

03:03.260 --> 03:04.910
<b>PLAN 13
TANPOPO</b>

03:04.910 --> 03:09.370
<b>The optical storage device that
you acquired from the former spy, Kurogao,</b>

03:09.810 --> 03:11.650
<b>according to my analysis,</b>

03:11.650 --> 03:16.440
<b>contains the guest list
for a Yozakura wedding reception.</b>

03:16.440 --> 03:17.940
<b>Reception?</b>

03:17.940 --> 03:19.090
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:19.090 --> 03:20.860
<b>9TH YOZAKURA HEAD'S WEDDING RECEPTION</b>

03:20.860 --> 03:22.180
<b>The ninth head's, no less.</b>

03:22.390 --> 03:26.140
<b>In other words,
our parents' wedding reception.</b>

03:26.140 --> 03:27.750
<b>Huh?</b>

03:27.750 --> 03:30.000
<b>Most of the attendees
were civilians,</b>

03:30.000 --> 03:32.600
<b>so they must have held it
for the general public.</b>

03:33.250 --> 03:37.880
<b>For the Yozakuras, receptions are
just another ordinary task.</b>

03:38.290 --> 03:40.010
<b>The issue here...</b>

03:40.010 --> 03:41.180
<b>AKARI ASANO
HIDE ASANO</b>

03:41.180 --> 03:45.280
<b>...is the fact that your parents' names
are on this list.</b>

03:47.300 --> 03:50.310
<b>Can't draw any conclusions
from the guest list alone,</b>

03:50.310 --> 03:53.270
<b>but the one thing we know for sure
is that, before we were even born,</b>

03:53.270 --> 03:57.110
<b>there was a connection
between the Yozakuras and the Asanos.</b>

03:57.520 --> 03:59.480
<b>Is that right?</b>

04:00.360 --> 04:02.530
<b>You're accepting it just like that?</b>

04:02.530 --> 04:05.360
<b>No, I'm really stunned by this.</b>

04:05.780 --> 04:08.850
<b>It's just that when Kurogao told me...</b>

04:09.060 --> 04:13.040
<b>Hide Asano, Akari Asano,
Hikaru Asano...</b>

04:13.040 --> 04:16.360
<b>One rainy day,
they fell off a cliff, car and all.</b>

04:16.650 --> 04:19.760
<b>Your family died instantly,
but you alone survived.</b>

04:19.760 --> 04:21.590
<b>Truly miraculous.</b>

04:21.590 --> 04:22.990
<b>However...</b>

04:22.990 --> 04:28.600
<b>some miracles are the handiwork of man.</b>

04:29.630 --> 04:32.600
<b>Ever since then, I've been
mentally prepared for anything.</b>

04:32.970 --> 04:34.140
<b>So right now...</b>

04:35.930 --> 04:39.560
<b>I'm more worried about the person
beside me who's almost dying of shock.</b>

04:41.690 --> 04:43.570
<b>Let's get a divorce!</b>

04:43.570 --> 04:45.010
<b>Calm down, Mutsumi!</b>

04:45.010 --> 04:48.580
<b>I can't ever look you
in the eye again, Taiyo!</b>

04:48.580 --> 04:52.290
<b>I'm sure that because they got involved
with us, your family ended up--</b>

04:52.290 --> 04:55.420
<b>Hold up!
We can't be sure of that just yet!</b>

04:55.420 --> 04:58.300
<b>This info alone can't tell us
what really went down,</b>

04:58.300 --> 05:00.980
<b>and no matter what happened,
it was all in the past!</b>

05:02.130 --> 05:06.450
<b>I am who I am now all thanks to you.
Don't ever talk about breaking up.</b>

05:06.450 --> 05:08.470
<b>Taiyo!</b>

05:09.720 --> 05:12.430
<b>All right, all right. Get a room.</b>

05:13.010 --> 05:14.810
<b>But with all that being said,</b>

05:14.810 --> 05:19.380
<b>I want to know the truth
about what happened to my family.</b>

05:19.940 --> 05:24.110
<b>I know I'm just being selfish,
but if you wouldn't mind helping me--</b>

05:24.110 --> 05:26.820
<b>Hey, don't act like a stranger!
You're my kid brother!</b>

05:26.820 --> 05:28.010
<b>I'll poke your eyes out.</b>

05:28.010 --> 05:30.910
<b>You didn't have to prove it!</b>

05:30.910 --> 05:33.790
<b>The only thing is,
what are we going to do?</b>

05:33.790 --> 05:36.450
<b>To be honest, I'm stunned myself.</b>

05:36.870 --> 05:41.570
<b>All data on the former head should
have been wiped due to confidentiality.</b>

05:41.570 --> 05:44.760
<b>So the fact that this exists</b>

05:44.760 --> 05:48.200
<b>may mean that it's
an underworld-related matter.</b>

05:51.930 --> 05:55.440
<b>Meaning that it
might be worth it to go there.</b>

05:55.440 --> 05:56.520
<b>Go where?</b>

05:56.520 --> 06:00.130
<b>The organization that collects data
on those who've vanished without a trace.</b>

06:00.360 --> 06:02.020
<b>A place known as...</b>

06:02.020 --> 06:03.770
<b>the Library of the Dead.</b>

06:08.780 --> 06:11.660
<b>THE LIBRARY OF THE DEAD
SPY ASSOCIATION</b>

06:11.660 --> 06:12.890
<b>So, this is it?</b>

06:14.490 --> 06:16.540
<b>The Library of the Dead</b>

06:16.540 --> 06:19.410
<b>is a private organization
sponsored by the Spy Association.</b>

06:20.120 --> 06:22.330
<b>The information there is highly reliable.</b>

06:23.820 --> 06:25.780
<b>PLEASE TOUCH YOUR CARD</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.990
<b>You might find out the real reason
why your parents died.</b>

06:31.590 --> 06:33.450
<b>That said, watch your back.</b>

06:49.270 --> 06:52.010
<b>Could there be a lamer way to die?</b>

06:53.070 --> 06:55.660
<b>Please keep your voice down
in the library.</b>

06:57.820 --> 07:02.090
<b>We mustn't disturb the peaceful slumber
of the dead with the noise of the living.</b>

07:02.090 --> 07:03.690
<b>ME-CHAN
LIBRARIAN, SILVER-RANKED SPY</b>

07:07.960 --> 07:10.380
<b>Oh, man, this place is crazy!</b>

07:10.910 --> 07:14.010
<b>She loves and cares for the dead,</b>

07:14.010 --> 07:16.370
<b>so to make a sound in her castle
means death.</b>

07:16.970 --> 07:19.850
<b>The penalties depend on
the distance and volume,</b>

07:19.850 --> 07:22.020
<b>but sneezing in her ear is instant death.</b>

07:22.020 --> 07:24.190
<b>DAMAGE TO SIGHT AND HEARING /
DISMEMBERMENT / DEATH</b>

07:24.190 --> 07:26.090
<b>Death just for sneezing?</b>

07:26.090 --> 07:28.570
<b>She's Silver-ranked.</b>

07:28.570 --> 07:31.300
<b>She's not someone
you can defeat in a direct fight.</b>

07:32.070 --> 07:36.760
<b>What's really a pain
is that she patrols the facility silently.</b>

07:37.240 --> 07:40.910
<b>But as long as you don't make a sound,
you'll be fine.</b>

07:42.200 --> 07:44.460
<b>Even leakage from your earphones is risky.</b>

07:44.460 --> 07:46.770
<b>I'm going to direct you
at the lowest volume.</b>

07:47.010 --> 07:48.920
<b>Keep your head as you move about.</b>

07:52.590 --> 07:54.760
<b>Huh?
Your face is noisy.</b>

07:55.220 --> 07:58.450
<b>Me-chan! You have to admit
that's unreasonable!</b>

08:34.590 --> 08:36.890
<b>The categorization is
so complicated,</b>

08:36.890 --> 08:38.970
<b>I don't think I'll ever get anywhere.</b>

08:39.550 --> 08:41.830
<b>Let's see, next is...</b>

08:41.830 --> 08:45.310
<b>"Civilian, medical field,
within the last ten years,</b>

08:45.310 --> 08:47.900
<b>Japan, starts with A, male..."</b>

08:49.390 --> 08:50.570
<b>No way.</b>

08:55.900 --> 08:57.360
<b>For real?</b>

08:59.360 --> 09:02.500
<b>"Hide Asano.
Employed at a pharmaceutical company."</b>

09:02.500 --> 09:06.650
<b>"Wife: Akari. Eldest son: Taiyo.
Second son: Hikaru."</b>

09:06.880 --> 09:14.010
<b>"Fell to his death while driving through
Karizakura Pass on June 6. Age 39."</b>

09:14.010 --> 09:18.120
<b>There's no information
on what caused the accident.</b>

09:18.840 --> 09:21.930
<b>I can't believe I came all this way
only to find nothing.</b>

09:23.300 --> 09:24.890
<b>Wait, this must be...</b>

09:25.640 --> 09:29.150
<b>a tablet-style insertion slot
for optical storage devices?</b>

09:30.060 --> 09:31.230
<b>Could it be...</b>

09:39.320 --> 09:42.030
<b>This isn't just a data storage device.</b>

09:42.030 --> 09:44.120
<b>It can also be used as a key!</b>

09:45.870 --> 09:50.330
<b>"All members of the Asano family
have been exterminated by Tanpopo."</b>

09:51.120 --> 09:53.730
<b>It wasn't... an accident!</b>

09:54.500 --> 09:55.670
<b>Tanpopo!</b>

09:56.710 --> 09:58.050
<b>UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS DETECTED</b>

10:02.080 --> 10:03.810
<b>Taiyo? What was that?</b>

10:03.810 --> 10:05.980
<b>The book blew up all of a sudden!</b>

10:05.980 --> 10:08.290
<b>You're in danger! Get out of there!</b>

10:09.310 --> 10:11.270
<b>Me-chan's on her way
from Corridor A-12!</b>

10:11.270 --> 10:12.250
<b>ETA is 6.5 seconds!</b>

10:12.250 --> 10:15.590
<b>At that volume, the mandatory
penalty level will be instant death!</b>

10:15.590 --> 10:19.340
<b>She'll go for your respiratory tract,
lungs, and upper torso! Meaning...</b>

10:20.150 --> 10:22.070
<b>just get down!
</b>

10:23.220 --> 10:27.440
<b>The memories of the dead
are being violated.</b>

10:28.640 --> 10:31.730
<b>North-northeast, 49 degrees, output 70%!</b>

10:32.250 --> 10:33.320
<b>Fire!</b>

10:39.630 --> 10:42.060
<b>The backup generator will start
in as soon as 20 seconds!</b>

10:42.060 --> 10:45.470
<b>Follow the wall to your right
and you'll get back to the entrance.</b>

10:47.910 --> 10:54.480
<b>Even without light, the sound
of your soul vibrates in my glass ears.</b>

10:54.480 --> 10:59.130
<b>Now, go to sleep... in my arms!</b>

10:59.130 --> 11:01.340
<b>She's nothing but a crazed tyrant!</b>

11:07.230 --> 11:11.080
<b>You can't beat her! Go back three steps
and enter the hole in the left corridor!</b>

11:12.810 --> 11:15.020
<b>Taiyo! Take off your earphones right now!</b>

11:15.020 --> 11:17.010
<b>Mutsumi?
 Do it now!</b>

11:17.010 --> 11:18.840
<b>I trust you. Mutsumi!</b>

11:20.700 --> 11:21.800
<b>VOLUME
SPEAKER</b>

11:30.760 --> 11:32.360
<b>I see!</b>

11:32.360 --> 11:36.360
<b>She's sensitive to sound, so she
couldn't withstand that loud noise.</b>

11:36.360 --> 11:40.200
<b>I thought that it might work
with Big Sis Shion's high-end earphones.</b>

11:40.200 --> 11:41.860
<b>Thanks, Mutsumi!</b>

11:42.980 --> 11:46.510
<b>It's just a single word,
but I have a clue now.</b>

11:48.910 --> 11:50.080
<b>Tanpopo!</b>

11:53.900 --> 11:55.170
<b>COMPLETE COLLECTION OF TORTURE</b>

11:55.170 --> 11:56.340
<b>I see.</b>

11:57.790 --> 11:59.760
<b>NANAO METAL
10X HARDER AND HEAVIER THAN IRON</b>

12:01.750 --> 12:03.180
<b>Tanpopo, eh?</b>

12:03.180 --> 12:04.760
<b>Interesting.
</b>

12:04.760 --> 12:07.850
<b>Hey, do you think
this will get us anywhere?</b>

12:07.850 --> 12:12.150
<b>Who would have thought that your family
also fell victim to Tanpopo?</b>

12:12.150 --> 12:13.290
<b>Huh?</b>

12:13.290 --> 12:16.020
<b>What do you mean, also?</b>

12:17.690 --> 12:21.340
<b>They also killed Mutsumi's mother,
the previous head.</b>

12:23.480 --> 12:28.120
<b>I've taken full advantage of
every information network at our disposal,</b>

12:28.120 --> 12:31.020
<b>but I still haven't
been able to catch them.</b>

12:31.490 --> 12:35.840
<b>All I know is that it's one of
the organizations targeting Mutsumi,</b>

12:35.840 --> 12:38.340
<b>and that it's an extremely powerful one.</b>

12:39.080 --> 12:42.590
<b>And that its agents
all have a dandelion tattoo.</b>

12:43.750 --> 12:46.560
<b>Rage, hatred, irritation...
</b>

12:46.560 --> 12:50.390
<b>For years, I've been letting
these negative feelings fester.</b>

12:51.000 --> 12:53.140
<b>You know how that feels, too, right?</b>

12:53.140 --> 12:56.060
<b>The feeling of loss
after losing your family!</b>

12:56.060 --> 12:58.190
<b>I get it! I get it! I get it! I do get it!</b>

12:58.190 --> 13:02.090
<b>So please stop
taking it out on me!</b>

13:02.650 --> 13:07.930
<b>However, I've made some progress
thanks to the information you gleaned.</b>

13:09.150 --> 13:12.040
<b>Your family
fell victim to Tanpopo,</b>

13:12.040 --> 13:16.290
<b>and your father was an office worker
in the medical field.</b>

13:16.290 --> 13:18.250
<b>Based on those facts,</b>

13:18.250 --> 13:22.050
<b>I was able to narrow down my search
to the medical industry as a whole.</b>

13:22.050 --> 13:25.660
<b>Which led to the discovery
of some truly interesting data.</b>

13:25.660 --> 13:28.560
<b>In the month before and after
the Asano family's accident,</b>

13:28.560 --> 13:32.310
<b>fifteen people in the medical field
were killed in accidents.</b>

13:32.310 --> 13:38.100
<b>And a single man emerged
as the link between every one of them.</b>

13:38.680 --> 13:42.630
<b>The director of Kawashita Medical Clinic,
Makoto Kawashita.</b>

13:43.110 --> 13:44.900
<b>Makoto Kawashita?</b>

13:45.650 --> 13:47.070
<b>So this guy is...</b>

13:47.070 --> 13:49.700
<b>He's not necessarily
the mastermind behind it all.</b>

13:49.700 --> 13:52.810
<b>That said, there's no question
that he's a person of interest.</b>

13:53.200 --> 13:56.310
<b>The organization that killed
Mutsumi's mother, the ninth head,</b>

13:56.310 --> 13:58.210
<b>that killed your family,</b>

13:58.210 --> 14:03.000
<b>and is now extending its evil claws
towards Mutsumi, Tanpopo.</b>

14:07.250 --> 14:09.700
<b>Do you want
to expose the truth about them?</b>

14:14.010 --> 14:16.270
<b>I didn't even need to ask, did I?</b>

14:21.340 --> 14:23.300
<b>KAWASHITA MEDICAL CLINIC</b>

14:23.300 --> 14:25.860
<b>So this is Kawashita
Medical Clinic?</b>

14:25.860 --> 14:27.010
<b>Yes!</b>

14:27.440 --> 14:30.280
<b>Okay, we're going undercover, Taiyo!</b>

14:34.070 --> 14:37.330
<b>I've worn all kinds of disguises
up until now,</b>

14:37.330 --> 14:40.170
<b>but this may be
the most uncomfortable one of all.</b>

14:40.170 --> 14:43.880
<b>Now, now! You're a patient,
so you need to be slumped over more!</b>

14:43.880 --> 14:46.920
<b>He might know you, after all!</b>

14:46.920 --> 14:48.970
<b>You're Kousei Hirukawa, age 75,</b>

14:48.970 --> 14:51.680
<b>who transferred here
due to a chronic disease.</b>

14:51.680 --> 14:53.160
<b>And I...</b>

14:53.430 --> 14:56.230
<b>am your wife of 50 years,
who lives only for her husband!</b>

14:56.230 --> 14:58.600
<b>Mutsuko Hirukawa, age 75!</b>

14:58.600 --> 15:01.080
<b>You look like you're
enjoying this, Mutsumi!</b>

15:01.350 --> 15:04.090
<b>All right, here we go, darling!</b>

15:04.090 --> 15:08.050
<b>You're the one
who's way too spry for an old lady!</b>

15:10.900 --> 15:12.330
<b>Ugh.</b>

15:12.330 --> 15:14.200
<b>What's the matter, Taiyo?</b>

15:14.200 --> 15:16.750
<b>You look like
you're really not feeling well.</b>

15:16.750 --> 15:20.420
<b>It's not that I'm not feeling well.
These things are heavy.</b>

15:20.420 --> 15:21.480
<b>Huh?</b>

15:21.950 --> 15:25.670
<b>These weights will reproduce
the slow movements of an old man.</b>

15:25.670 --> 15:28.260
<b>Needless to say,
you have no right of refusal.</b>

15:29.090 --> 15:33.140
<b>Why is he hindering me like this
when I'm entering enemy territory?</b>

15:33.140 --> 15:35.850
<b>I'll have to
give him a talking-to</b>

15:35.850 --> 15:38.930
<b>about overstepping when we get home!</b>

15:38.930 --> 15:40.770
<b>Mr. Hirukawa?
 Uh?</b>

15:40.770 --> 15:42.270
<b>Mr. Kousei Hirukawa?</b>

15:49.480 --> 15:51.950
<b>E-Excuse me.</b>

15:52.820 --> 15:55.780
<b>Right this way, Mr. Hirukawa.</b>

15:59.660 --> 16:02.660
<b>So this is Makoto Kawashita?</b>

16:07.880 --> 16:11.550
<b>Mmm. Your chronic disease
seems to be under control.</b>

16:11.550 --> 16:13.590
<b>R-Right.</b>

16:13.590 --> 16:18.140
<b>But really, not a single
chipped tooth at your age! Well done, sir!</b>

16:18.140 --> 16:23.790
<b>Uh-- Thanks.
I-It's something I'm proud of.</b>

16:23.790 --> 16:26.730
<b>Compared to Dr. Yamashita,
who referred you to me,</b>

16:26.730 --> 16:30.860
<b>I've still got a long way to go,
but I'm going to give it my all.</b>

16:31.270 --> 16:34.140
<b>If anything comes up,
feel free to let me know!</b>

16:40.910 --> 16:43.580
<b>That doctor seemed so genuine...</b>

16:44.200 --> 16:46.900
<b>Here you go, honey! Say "ahh"!</b>

16:47.460 --> 16:49.500
<b>Mmm-hmm.
 Ahh...</b>

16:51.420 --> 16:53.380
<b>That's my darling!</b>

16:53.380 --> 16:56.620
<b>Take your time swallowing
so you don't choke.</b>

16:58.010 --> 17:01.390
<b>No one's around. I can feed myself.</b>

17:01.390 --> 17:05.080
<b>We're undercover.
We can't let down our guard.</b>

17:05.080 --> 17:07.540
<b>MANDARIN ORANGE JUICE</b>

17:08.730 --> 17:13.260
<b>I hope our golden years
are really as peaceful as this.</b>

17:13.690 --> 17:17.660
<b>With neither of us having anything to do
with assassinations or bounties</b>

17:17.660 --> 17:20.040
<b>and getting to be there
in each other's final moments.</b>

17:20.040 --> 17:23.450
<b>Not sure if that's a good or bad fate.</b>

17:27.160 --> 17:30.130
<b>But I think
I might like that, too.</b>

17:30.540 --> 17:33.090
<b>Growing old together in harmony,</b>

17:33.090 --> 17:36.700
<b>and one day, one of us will be there
in the other's final moments...</b>

17:37.210 --> 17:39.660
<b>I want you to see me off, Mutsumi.</b>

17:40.430 --> 17:46.020
<b>If you weren't around anymore,
I wouldn't know how to live after that.</b>

17:48.380 --> 17:50.480
<b>Taiyo!</b>

17:51.810 --> 17:54.910
<b>One more time!
Please utter that line one more time!</b>

17:54.910 --> 17:57.780
<b>I don't know what you're
talking about! I never said a thing!</b>

18:00.300 --> 18:02.270
<b>KAWASHITA MEDICAL CLINIC</b>

18:02.270 --> 18:07.730
<b>DIRECTOR'S OFFICE</b>

18:08.620 --> 18:12.960
<b>Okay, Dr. Tanaka,
I'm leaving the rest to you!</b>

18:12.960 --> 18:15.590
<b>Thank you
for your hard work, Director.</b>

18:15.590 --> 18:17.180
<b>Right, see you!</b>

18:41.530 --> 18:43.580
<b>DIRECTOR'S OFFICE</b>

18:50.370 --> 18:53.440
<b>At a glance, it looks like
any old doctor's computer.</b>

18:54.170 --> 18:57.300
<b>But there are empty folders
that seem out of place,</b>

18:57.300 --> 18:58.910
<b>passwords at every level,</b>

18:59.510 --> 19:00.970
<b>and fingerprint ID.</b>

19:04.260 --> 19:08.890
<b>If I scan the hard drive using
Big Sis Shion's analytical program...</b>

19:09.330 --> 19:10.770
<b>SCANNING</b>

19:10.770 --> 19:13.340
<b>...it will reveal the encrypted data!</b>

19:13.340 --> 19:14.300
<b>SOMEI-YOSHINO PROJECT OVERVIEW</b>

19:14.610 --> 19:17.400
<b>"The Somei-yoshino Project"?</b>

19:19.260 --> 19:21.620
<b>The Yozakura spy family.</b>

19:21.620 --> 19:25.580
<b>A distinguished underworld family that has
produced generations of talented spies.</b>

19:25.580 --> 19:29.580
<b>But its biological mechanism
is exceedingly simple.</b>

19:30.290 --> 19:34.960
<b>The protein called someinine found
in the blood of the Yozakura head</b>

19:34.960 --> 19:38.840
<b>increases cell division speed
and the threshold of division.</b>

19:38.840 --> 19:41.760
<b>This is the source
of the Yozakura family's</b>

19:41.760 --> 19:44.160
<b>enhanced five senses
and physical abilities.</b>

19:44.760 --> 19:46.480
<b>This someinine is also effective</b>

19:46.480 --> 19:50.520
<b>even when ingested
by those outside the Yozakura family.</b>

19:50.520 --> 19:56.250
<b>For this reason, Yozakura blood is noted
as an extremely powerful doping agent.</b>

19:56.650 --> 20:02.070
<b>Yozakura blood...
an extremely powerful doping agent?</b>

20:03.220 --> 20:07.080
<b>Unfortunately, someinine
cannot be created synthetically.</b>

20:07.080 --> 20:10.500
<b>Therefore, in order to mass-produce it
as a bioweapon,</b>

20:10.500 --> 20:16.130
<b>as well as build a distribution network,
we would need a someinine factory.</b>

20:16.130 --> 20:17.300
<b>In other words...</b>

20:17.730 --> 20:20.700
<b>Mutsumi Yozakura's heart.</b>

20:34.350 --> 20:38.050
<b>Whoops, I thought there was a rat in here.</b>

20:38.690 --> 20:42.190
<b>Wow, I'd heard the rumors
that you were alive,</b>

20:42.610 --> 20:46.330
<b>but I never dreamed
that you'd make your way here.</b>

20:46.330 --> 20:48.740
<b>Life is just full of surprises!</b>

20:48.740 --> 20:54.540
<b>Did you kill Mutsumi's mother
and my family?</b>

20:54.540 --> 20:58.270
<b>What good would it
do you to know such trivial facts?</b>

20:58.270 --> 21:03.680
<b>Neither a mere individual like you,
nor a clan like the Yozakuras,</b>

21:03.680 --> 21:06.120
<b>have any chance of stopping us.</b>

21:08.800 --> 21:13.370
<b>If you hadn't contemplated revenge,
you could have lived a little bit longer.</b>

21:16.500 --> 21:18.960
<b>I couldn't care less
about revenge!</b>

21:19.520 --> 21:22.720
<b>All I want is to protect Mutsumi!</b>

21:26.180 --> 21:27.350
<b>It doesn't work on him?</b>

21:28.300 --> 21:31.020
<b>You got an extension on that life...</b>

21:32.810 --> 21:34.370
<b>so take good care of it.</b>

21:44.130 --> 21:45.720
<b>He got away!</b>

21:47.840 --> 21:49.760
<b>Along with the computer!</b>

21:53.180 --> 21:56.500
<b>But I'd already extracted that data.</b>

21:58.100 --> 22:00.400
<b>I've found out one part of their scheme.</b>

22:01.270 --> 22:04.610
<b>For Mutsumi's sake,
I'm going to expose them, no matter what.</b>

22:05.650 --> 22:07.010
<b>Tanpopo.</b>

22:08.900 --> 22:10.660
<b>And Makoto Kawashita!</b>

23:41.940 --> 23:46.960
<b>NEXT TIME
AIM FOR THE SUITE ROOM</b>
